body:

### Hi there :)

I’m Olena, a Software Engineer with 3 years of experience building backend systems, covering the full cycle: from architecture and development to testing and deployment.

Learning was always an integral part of my life. I’ve spent a significant part of my career in data analysis and research. Also, I had familiarity with scientific activity during my studying at university. So, my job expertise contributed the habit to study constantly and search insights. Beyond daily projects, I grow by contributing to open source, attending conferences and meetups, and being part of the Python community.

What I love most about this work is that there’s always something new to learn. I believe that *learning in public* leads to deeper understanding. Writing forces you to clarify your thinking, and sharing it might help someone else along the way. That’s why this blog exists.

Here I write about:

- Git workflows and best practices for effective collaboration.
- Python core: internals, patterns, and idiomatic code.
- Testing strategies: what to test, how to structure tests, and what actually works.
- Automating and deploying: CI/CD, Docker, GitHub Actions, and infrastructure as code.

*You can find my open source work and projects on [GitHub](https://github.com/OlenaYefymenko).*

Outside of work, I enjoy staying active: hiking, cycling, and skiing in winter. Besides that, dance has always been part of my life — I studied choreography for years and still can't resist a good song!
